.TH EPIGRAPH-WALL 1 "September 2026" "Version 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
epigraph-wall \- stealth in-memory wallpaper injector for Hyprland
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B epigraph-wall
[\fB\-l\fR] [\fB\-n\fR \fIname\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B epigraph-wall
injects high-resolution, LaTeX-typeset epigraph wallpapers directly into
Hyprland (\fBhyprpaper\fR) from RAM without touching physical storage.
Images are pre-compiled into the binary using Go embedding and exposed via
the Linux \fBmemfd_create\fR(2) system call.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-l
List all embedded epigraph image names.
.TP
.BI \-n \ name
Specify the image name to apply (e.g. \fI01_sovereignty.png\fR). Defaults to a random selection.
.SH EXAMPLES
Apply a random embedded epigraph:
.IP
.nf
epigraph-wall
.fi
.PP
List and pick a specific wallpaper:
.IP
.nf
epigraph-wall -l
epigraph-wall -n 01_sovereignty.png
.fi
.SH AUTHOR
Crafted for sovereign POSIX environments.
